PPA's deflate recipes (pas/ppapreflate.pas, pas/ppacorr.pas,
doc/PREFLATE.md) take the idea of rebuilding a deflate stream from the bytes
it holds and a small description of its encoder's work, flushes included,
and (kind 3) of a predictor that follows the stream's own parse and of
coding a match's distance as its rank among the candidates, from preflate by Dirk
Steinke (Apache-2.0; studied as 0.3.4, from precomp 0.4.7's
contrib/preflate). No code of preflate is in PPA; tools/preflate uses a
preflate binary built outside the repository only as a yardstick.

Kind 3's guesses of a block's code lengths and of their run-length coding
(pas/ppacorr.pas, "tree builders") reproduce what other encoders do, each
written in our own code from how that encoder works, to give the same
lengths:
  - libdeflate (Eric Biggers, MIT): deflate_make_huffman_code (its sort, its
    two-queue tree, its length limit) and deflate_compute_precode_items;
  - miniz (Rich Geldreich and contributors, MIT / Unlicense):
    tdefl_optimize_huffman_table (with Alistair Moffat and Jyrki
    Katajainen's in-place code lengths) and tdefl_start_dynamic_block's
    run-length coding;
  - zopfli (Copyright 2011 Google Inc., Apache License 2.0): length-limited
    lengths by package-merge (our own, classic, package-merge), its
    PatchDistanceCodesForBuggyDecoders, its 8 run-length codings of
    EncodeTree, and OptimizeHuffmanForRle, whose steps EvenForRle follows
    one by one (Apache License 2.0: http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

pas/ppaminiz.pas and pas/ppaminizc.c (the deflate recipes of kind 2,
doc/PREFLATE.md) are a port to FreePascal and C of the parts of miniz's
tdefl (miniz 1.14 and 3.0.2) that decide its choices: tdefl_compress_normal,
tdefl_compress_fast, tdefl_find_match and tdefl_flush_block's choice of a
block's codes, so that PPA can tell a stream miniz wrote by its flags.
